# Reasoning with a quoted belief
#
# Einstein says "not all that glitters is gold", written as a quoted rule.
# Everyone believes what Einstein says, and what he says is true. eyeron
# derives that Fabian believes the quoted rule, and, by applying that rule
# once it is asserted, that the north star is not necessarily gold. Shows
# quoted formulas as values of variables, a rule whose conclusion is a
# variable (=> ?phi), and a backward rule (<=) answered on demand.

@base <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eye/reasoning/qiana/qiana.n3> .
@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/ns#> .

# forall phi, x: says(Einstein, phi) => believes(x, phi)
# A backward rule: it is used only when a query asks who believes what
{
    ?x :believes ?phi
} <= {
    :Einstein :says ?phi
} .

# forall phi: says(Einstein, phi) => phi
# The quoted formula itself is asserted, so a quoted rule becomes a live rule
{
    :Einstein :says ?phi
} => ?phi .

# says(Einstein, not (forall x: glitters(x) => gold(x)))
:Einstein :says {
    {
        ?x a :glitter
    } => {
        ?x :notNecessarilyA :gold
    }
} .

# The north star glitters
:northStar a :glitter .

# Queries: what Fabian believes, and what is not necessarily what
@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/ns#> .
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .

{
    :Fabian :believes ?what .
} log:query {
    :Fabian :believes ?what .
} .

{
    ?x :notNecessarilyA ?what .
} log:query {
    ?x :notNecessarilyA ?what .
} .
